# What the Canon does not Govern.
#
# Same Syntax as .gitignore, and git itself Reads it:
#   git ls-files --cached  --ignored --exclude-from=.canonignore
#   git ls-files --others  --ignored --exclude-from=.canonignore
#
# .gitignore Says what the Repository does not Carry.
# This Says what the Repository Carries but does not Teach.
# An Agent may Read every Path here. It must never Copy one.

# The Counter-Example. Every Rule here is Broken on Purpose,
# and its README Names which Rule each Break Earned.
examples/school/java-before/**
!examples/school/java-before/README.md

# Raw Context, not yet Distilled. Notes in Progress, never Instructions.
STORY.md
stories/**
chaos/**
CHAOS.md

# Vendored and Generated. Present on Disk, Written by no one here.
**/node_modules/**
**/dist/**
**/target/**
**/bin/**
**/.mvn/**
mvnw
mvnw.cmd
**/go.sum
**/package-lock.json
